1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:02,286
A pipe bursts at midnight.

2
00:00:02,286 --> 00:00:04,258
A gamer wants a new console today.

3
00:00:04,258 --> 00:00:06,999
A family needs groceries from the shop down the street.

4
00:00:06,999 --> 00:00:10,406
Three different businesses, and the same story every time:

5
00:00:10,406 --> 00:00:13,284
calls that go unanswered, prices nobody confirms,

6
00:00:13,284 --> 00:00:15,364
and promises that never show up.

7
00:00:15,816 --> 00:00:18,314
Across Pakistan, small businesses still run

8
00:00:18,314 --> 00:00:19,998
on phone calls and guesswork.

9
00:00:19,998 --> 00:00:22,205
Customers can't see who they're dealing with,

10
00:00:22,205 --> 00:00:24,264
what it will cost, or when it will arrive.

11
00:00:24,264 --> 00:00:28,690
Businesses juggle orders and jobs across WhatsApp chats and notebooks.

12
00:00:28,690 --> 00:00:30,106
And the staff doing the work

13
00:00:30,106 --> 00:00:32,079
have no record of the jobs they finish,

14
00:00:32,079 --> 00:00:33,443
or the trust they earn.

15
00:00:33,910 --> 00:00:35,236
This is FleetOS.

16
00:00:35,236 --> 00:00:37,416
One platform that connects three people

17
00:00:37,416 --> 00:00:39,149
around every job: the customer,

18
00:00:39,149 --> 00:00:41,497
the business that serves them, and a super

19
00:00:41,497 --> 00:00:43,877
admin who keeps the marketplace honest.

20
00:00:44,348 --> 00:00:46,087
And it isn't built for one trade.

21
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:48,209
FleetOS is a SaaS platform.

22
00:00:48,209 --> 00:00:51,458
Plumbers, gaming and electronics stores, local shops,

23
00:00:51,458 --> 00:00:54,769
salons, restaurants: each business picks its category,

24
00:00:54,769 --> 00:00:57,589
and gets a workspace that speaks its language.

25
00:00:57,589 --> 00:00:59,969
It starts with small and medium businesses,

26
00:00:59,969 --> 00:01:01,740
and it's built to scale to large

27
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:05,427
private limited companies, across Pakistan and internationally.

28
00:01:05,898 --> 00:01:07,247
It starts with the customer.

29
00:01:07,247 --> 00:01:10,167
They search approved businesses by city and service,

30
00:01:10,167 --> 00:01:11,852
compare ratings, and book with

31
00:01:11,852 --> 00:01:14,523
a clear price, before anything is confirmed.

32
00:01:14,992 --> 00:01:17,350
The request reaches the business instantly.

33
00:01:17,350 --> 00:01:19,275
The team can accept it, or decline it

34
00:01:19,275 --> 00:01:21,513
with a reason the customer sees right away.

35
00:01:21,513 --> 00:01:24,730
Smart Dispatch then suggests the best staff member,

36
00:01:24,730 --> 00:01:27,516
ranked by distance, workload, and rating.

37
00:01:27,974 --> 00:01:30,023
Now the customer watches the job move.

38
00:01:30,023 --> 00:01:32,122
The plumber is en route, and the arrival

39
00:01:32,122 --> 00:01:34,117
time counts down live on their screen.

40
00:01:34,117 --> 00:01:34,931
Arrived.

41
00:01:34,931 --> 00:01:35,963
In progress.

42
00:01:35,963 --> 00:01:36,777
Completed.

43
00:01:36,777 --> 00:01:40,096
Every step updates for everyone, at the same moment.

44
00:01:40,548 --> 00:01:42,997
When the work is done, the payment is recorded,

45
00:01:42,997 --> 00:01:44,091
an invoice is issued,

46
00:01:44,091 --> 00:01:46,018
and the customer leaves a rating that

47
00:01:46,018 --> 00:01:48,198
helps good workers win their next job.

48
00:01:48,658 --> 00:01:51,146
Behind it all, the super admin reviews every

49
00:01:51,146 --> 00:01:53,464
business's documents before it goes live,

50
00:01:53,464 --> 00:01:57,026
watches jobs and payments across the platform, handles support,

51
00:01:57,026 --> 00:01:59,714
and can suspend anyone who breaks the rules.

52
00:02:00,176 --> 00:02:02,959
Under the hood, it's a full MERN stack.

53
00:02:02,959 --> 00:02:05,803
MongoDB is the single source of truth.

54
00:02:05,803 --> 00:02:09,277
Express and Node power a secure, role-based API.

55
00:02:09,277 --> 00:02:11,789
React drives three fast portals.

56
00:02:11,789 --> 00:02:15,922
And Socket.IO keeps every screen in sync, in real time.

57
00:02:16,374 --> 00:02:17,494
So, what changes?

58
00:02:17,494 --> 00:02:19,982
Customers get transparency and safety.

59
00:02:19,982 --> 00:02:22,217
Workers get a digital record of their work,

60
00:02:22,217 --> 00:02:24,764
a reputation they can build, and steadier income.

61
00:02:24,764 --> 00:02:27,474
Businesses trade paperwork for a live workspace,

62
00:02:27,474 --> 00:02:29,959
and reach customers they never could before.

63
00:02:29,959 --> 00:02:33,252
And every payment is documented, moving the informal

64
00:02:33,252 --> 00:02:36,111
economy one step closer to the formal one.

65
00:02:36,556 --> 00:02:38,123
And this is only version one.

66
00:02:38,123 --> 00:02:42,061
Next up: mobile wallet payments like JazzCash and Easypaisa,

67
00:02:42,061 --> 00:02:43,899
Urdu and regional languages,

68
00:02:43,899 --> 00:02:47,246
a staff app with live GPS, SMS and WhatsApp alerts,

69
00:02:47,246 --> 00:02:49,940
and verified skill badges for workers.

70
00:02:50,402 --> 00:02:51,350
FleetOS.

71
00:02:51,350 --> 00:02:54,056
Every service job, from request to receipt.

72
00:02:54,056 --> 00:02:55,974
Designed and built end to end,

73
00:02:55,974 --> 00:02:58,476
from the database to the last pixel.
